{
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Waddington-OT 使用时间进程中的单细胞表达谱快照来推断细胞的可能来源与命运。",
      "basis": "KG_GROUNDED",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 2,
          "quote": "Here, we describe a conceptual framework, implemented in a method called Waddington-OT, that aims to capture the notion that\ncells at any time are drawn from a probability distribution in gene-expression space, and each cell has a\ndistribution of both probable origins and probable fates (Figure 1). It uses\nscRNA-seq data collected across a time-course to infer how these probability distributions evolve over time, by using the mathematical\napproach of Optimal Transport (OT)."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "该方法要求输入为时间进程中的单细胞表达谱，并需要采样时间元数据。",
      "basis": "KG_GROUNDED",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 1,
          "quote": "It uses scRNA-seq data collected across a time-course to infer how these probability distributions evolve over time, by using the mathematical approach of Optimal Transport (OT)."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "你提供的条件满足“每个时间点都有单细胞表达谱”和“四个有序时间点”，因此从输入形式上看与该方法的时间进程快照要求一致。",
      "basis": "USER_PROVIDED_FACT",
      "citations": [],
      "context_fact_ids": [
        "user:expression_profiles",
        "user:sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "但现有证据只说明该方法使用时间进程快照，并未明确四个时间点是否足够，也未说明时间间隔或细胞数量等具体采样设计要求。",
      "basis": "MODEL_KNOWLEDGE",
      "citations": [],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "提醒：该方法通过最优传输推断的是概率性时间耦合，并非对同一细胞的直接物理追踪，因此“来源与命运”是概率推断而非确定性谱系追踪。",
      "basis": "CAUTION_CONTEXT",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 5,
          "quote": "because different cells are sampled independently at different time points, we lose the joint distribution of expression between\npairs of time points, called temporal coupling. Absent any constraint on cellular transitions, we cannot infer\nthe temporal coupling, but if we assume that cells move short distances over short time periods, then we can infer the temporal\ncoupling by using the mathematical technique of optimal transport"
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "提醒：该方法隐含马尔可夫假设，即细胞命运只取决于当前位置而非历史，且只捕捉分布中随时间变化的部分，这会影响对长时程来源与命运推断的解释。",
      "basis": "CAUTION_CONTEXT",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 4,
          "quote": "The optimal-transport\ncalculation (i) implicitly assumes that a cell’s fate depends on its current position but not on its previous history\n(i.e., the stochastic process is Markov) and (ii) captures only the time-varying components of the distribution (see Discussion)."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "clarification": null
}
